WEBVTT

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:38.810
Speaking of job interviews,

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:39.410
Yes?

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:44.330
there was this one incident where an interviewer from Nissan asked, "What does GNP stand for?"

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:49.000
The applicant answered,
"Go, Nissan Pulsar!" and was hired.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.550
There was another case where an applicant was
late for an interview at a convenience store chain,

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:57.470
but as soon as he said, "I'm glad it's always open, Lawson!",
the interviewer laughed and hired him on the spot.

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:01.090
That's practically an urban legend.

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:06.710
Yeah. Those kinds of stories are more
painful than they are funny right now.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:11.020
What's wrong?

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:16.920
I was at an interview the other day,
and they were seeing people in groups of three to four.

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:21.780
There was this idiotic jock sitting next to me,

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:25.470
probably the son of a shop owner.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:29.990
The interviewer said,
"K, tell me about your lineage"

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:31.000
Uh-huh.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:38.380
and he replied, "Ka ki ku ke ko."

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:43.760
In other words, he confused lineage with the K linage.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.630
I don't know if that was because he was nervous, but...

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:49.520
Oh, I get it.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.180
Well, it wasn't very funny.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:56.240
I can't really comment on it either way.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:03.260
The interviewer laughed hysterically. The idiot
knew he received a favorable reaction and played along.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:09.230
He was beaming with a sense of satisfaction,
leaving the rest of us in a state of bewilderment.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.460
That must have been an awkward situation.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:17.950
I really messed up because of him. I'm not sure whether I should take these interviews seriously or try to get a reaction.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:20.990
The logical answer would be to take it seriously.

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.210
I see.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:26.420
You're right.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.680
Did you try to get a reaction out of the interviewer?

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.410
You shouldn't attempt to do
something you're not accustomed to doing.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:39.440
I refuse to accept failure on account of my inexperience.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:46.950
Well, they say naturals will always beat geniuses.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:51.410
It's not like I'm a genius or a natural, though.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:54.660
Now, now. It's a little too early to be worried.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:56.600
With that said, I'll hand this to you.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:59.710
You're suggesting that I read this and check it out.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:01.780
In addition to that, I should participate in it.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.270
Aren't you going?

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:05.770
Well, I am.

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:10.180
You look like a typical otaku salaryman in that suit and the catalog in hand.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:14.270
Get off my back. I'm not even at the level of a salaryman yet.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:18.000
The upcoming Comifes will only be two days long, right?

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.230
Do we have any plans for this one?

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.370
The usual, I guess.

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:31.320
We'll go shopping as a group on the final day,
but attendance during the first day will be optional.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:34.780
Ohno-san, you can cosplay on the final day if you'd like to.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.300
Thanks.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:40.520
A lot of friends and people will be there after all.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:44.380
I'll do my shopping on the first day,
so let me know if anything comes up.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.270
Are Kugayama and the others coming?

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:51.190
I haven't heard from them yet. Should I call them?

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.640
I see. I'd appreciate it.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.970
Ogiue-san, are you going to attend the first day?

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:01.250
No, I won't.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:04.190
I don't want to be in a place plagued with that much appetence.

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:11.460
Oh, is that so? Isn't this coming from
someone who's already participated in a circle entry?

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:14.750
I was obligated to participate as a member of Genshiken.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:18.320
It's not like it concerns me.
To each her own.

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:20.350
I'll attend on the final day.

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:22.890
The more people there are, the better.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:27.340
You should attend both days, Ogiue-san.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:30.060
It's not like you'll have to stick around Ohno-san or anyone else.

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:33.850
I think it'll be more fun
to attend than not to.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:40.660
Besides, if you're thinking about participating as a circle member in the future, it's better to have more experience.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:41.810
Oh?

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:45.790
That was just a rumor that
Kasukabe-senpai was spreading about me.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:49.280
Would you stop making those sarcastic nods?

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:55.220
It should go without saying that participating as a circle
and as an individual are two completely different things.

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:57.480
It's okay, Sasahara-san.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:59.480
You don't have to convince her any further.

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:02.570
She'll definitely be there. You don't have to worry about a thing.

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:04.180
I will not!

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:08.130
Oh, is that so?

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:13.460
The kinds of things you enjoy, like Scrum Dunk, will be available on the first day, Ogiue-san.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:14.600
Really?

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:19.090
Your personal favorite, Reass Mood,
will be there, too.

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:21.310
H-How did you know that?

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:24.100
It's hardly a secret.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:29.400
Whenever you look at Reass-related items,
it's like your eyes turn into that of a wolf.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:31.610
You're lying!

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:34.900
Well, I understand how you feel.

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:37.610
Navels are luscious, aren't they?

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.410
I don't know what you're talking about!

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:44.350
Oh, but you're not going on the first day, are you?

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:46.150
What a pity.

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:47.300
I'm not going!

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.510
Oh?

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:49.700
I'm not going!

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:50.760
Oh?

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:53.010
I definitely won't go!

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:03.940
<i>This hairstyle and these glasses remind me
of what I looked like in high school.</i>

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:08.930
<i>My old clothes make me look like a
female otaku straight out of the country,</i>

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:13.010
<i>not that I can deny that fact.</i>

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:18.190
<i>Even if I run into someone from
Genshiken, no one will be able to recognize me.</i>

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:20.820
<i>Hey, I shouldn't be wasting my time thinking about that.</i>

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:22.420
<i>Why the hell...</i>

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:24.500
...was I forced to do this?!

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.960
Damn that Ohno!

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:32.850
This year looks pretty bad.

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:35.650
Do you think the anime bubble will burst?

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:38.720
How long have they been saying that it'd burst this year?

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:41.890
It's obvious that the winner takes all in this industry.

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:46.140
Well, wasn't Gangaru Bleed like that?

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:50.280
Interest died as quickly as it was
generated. Is that a healthy trend?

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:51.890
It's all about sales.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:55.380
Ow...

00:07:57.070 --> 00:08:00.730
The maid cafe in Nishi Shinjuku became a ramen shop.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:04.750
Are you talking about the area
where stores keep opening and closing?

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:08.430
Yeah.
I don't know whether I should say finally or good riddance.

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:09.850
<i>Their perfume stinks.</i>

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:16.010
<i>What's with that paper bag?
Did he bring that on the train? How shameless.</i>

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:18.220
Wow, the quality is amazing!

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:19.900
Agreed, agreed.

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:22.800
<i>Don't read it on the street!
How embarrassing.</i>

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:27.280
<i>There are too many people here!</i>

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:29.070
<i>I can't stand it!</i>

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.030
<i>It stinks, too!</i>

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:34.160
<i>How frustrating!</i>

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:39.830
<i>Why the hell am I stuck here among a herd of otakus?</i>

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.580
<i>I demand an explanation!</i>

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:48.670
<i>On that note, what's with this weather? It's too hot!</i>

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:50.990
<i>It's winter, for crying out loud!</i>

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:52.630
<i>Temperatures should be lower!</i>

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:56.100
<i>This is unacceptable. Completely unacceptable!</i>

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:58.320
<i>I'm pissed. I'm pissed!</i>

00:08:58.710 --> 00:08:59.860
<i>I'm pissed.</i>

00:08:59.860 --> 00:09:01.370
One copy, please.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.390
<i>I'm really pissed off!</i>

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:05.570
I'd like a copy of this and that.

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:07.200
<i>I'm incredibly pissed!</i>

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:09.860
Please give me a copy of all the new books!

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:19.700
I've finished looking through the absolute purchase field, but...

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:30.080
Let's take a look around the secondary absolute purchase field.

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:34.220
We'll meet at the usual place at 2 P.M., okay?

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:35.060
Got it.

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:37.200
You've got to get "Nurehen" no matter what.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:37.880
Three copies.

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:39.580
I know.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:43.400
Make sure you get as many of the
"Usurper of the Empire" books as you can.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:46.710
Doesn't it seem like Yabusaki's
always doing everything by herself?

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:48.980
How does she stay so calm?
There's no way I could do that.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:52.090
She must have a lot of confidence.
How cool.

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:54.910
Is that supposed to make me feel better?

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:59.270
To those of you standing in line,
please move forward whenever you can.

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:04.120
One copy...

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:05.910
Can I have a copy of the new book?

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:09.340
<i>O-Ogiue?</i>

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:15.800
Why the hell is Ogiue buying an Empire book?

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:18.240
Do you have any new titles?

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:19.720
<i>Her again?</i>

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:22.930
<i>What does Ogiue want an AIUE book for?</i>

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:25.770
One copy, please.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:27.840
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:33.530
<i>How did she know about "Futomomo"? It was supposed to be a sleeper hit.</i>

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:34.550
<i>Hey!</i>

00:10:34.550 --> 00:10:37.170
Sorry, we just sold out.

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:44.990
<i>What's going on? What is she up to?</i>

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:48.050
I'd like an application form, please.

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:50.820
<i>Geez, I'm running out of time.</i>

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:52.670
<i>I'll never hear the end of their complaints.</i>

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:03.930
Let's go to the West Building.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:09.260
I felt a little guilty since it was like cheating the others.

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:12.610
The people who were standing in line all
glared at us as if to ask, "Who the hell are you?"

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:15.020
It would have been rude if we didn't accept it.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:20.360
It'd be impolite if I came and
didn't say hello to people I knew, but...

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:24.250
Why don't you make another book? You could return the favor to them.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:26.210
Well...

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:42.040
<i>What the hell am I doing?</i>

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:43.350
You should make more books
while you still have some free time.

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:44.720
<i>Stop it, you're too close.</i>

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:47.140
Is that so? I thought that the people who do
these kinds of things end up doing it forever.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:49.210
<i>They really won't notice, will they?</i>

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:51.640
Well, we're not like them,

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:52.770
Yeah.

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:54.840
which is why it makes more sense to do it now.

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:57.400
In that case, you should do it, Kousaka-kun.

00:11:57.680 --> 00:11:59.410
I'm only good at setting the mood.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.370
<i>Now that I've come this far...</i>

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:07.710
<i>They're probably waiting for
Ohno-senpai to finish changing anyway.</i>

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:09.970
<i>I might as well stay put until she comes back.</i>

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:13.660
Kousaka, have you played any interesting games lately?

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:17.380
Let's see. "Maimai" was pretty good.

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:19.970
Was it from the same developer as Menma?

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:24.340
Yeah. One of their artists left, so I was a little worried,

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:26.630
but the scenario made up for it.

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:28.640
That doesn't sound very encouraging.

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:31.420
Can I borrow it when you're finished?

00:12:31.420 --> 00:12:33.230
Sure, I'll bring it tomorrow.

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:36.000
It was just released the day before yesterday!

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:38.050
You didn't waste any time clearing it, did you?

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:40.450
I have more than enough games to play.

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:43.970
I'm satisfied with beating the game for the time being.

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:45.440
Oh, really?

00:12:45.440 --> 00:12:49.160
If you're talking about usability, "Green Door" is better.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:50.460
Usability?

00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:53.410
<i>They're being really candid!</i>

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:56.860
Aren't there grotesque torture scenes in that game?

00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:59.180
I'm not really into that.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.420
You're the naïve type, aren't you?

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:06.510
I developed a trauma to those kinds of things ever
since I saw a friend's erotic manga in middle school.

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:08.130
Did it involve erotic cruelty?

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:11.410
Yeah. It also had a father and daughter incest plot.

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:13.950
Wow, I know what you mean.

00:13:13.950 --> 00:13:16.670
I'm more interested in the ones
that are just as funny as they are erotic.

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:19.000
I like depressing stories,

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.950
like the ending where everyone dies in "Jukkai".

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.170
Well, I'm Sasahara the wuss.

00:13:24.170 --> 00:13:29.370
I get it. You don't like titles that feature sadistic male leads, but you don't mind if the female lead is like that.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:32.070
Oh, like Reika from "Daymare".

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:35.500
Oh, the chainsaw girl.

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:45.000
She's ill-tempered, but she laughs
hysterically when she has a weapon in her hand.

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:46.660
She's sort of like Ogiue-san.

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:47.720
What?

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:51.120
They're both the small, tsundere type.

00:13:52.300 --> 00:13:54.760
<i>Why are they talking about me?</i>

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:56.970
She should have come today.

00:13:56.970 --> 00:14:00.830
She's fit in better as of late
compared to when she first joined the club.

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:02.120
You're right.

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:05.960
She's now at a level where she
can evenly quarrel with Ohno-san.

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:08.020
Yeah, sorry about that.

00:14:08.020 --> 00:14:10.040
You don't have to apologize, Tanaka-san.

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:11.900
Well, I'm really sorry.

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:13.440
Did that upset you?

00:14:13.440 --> 00:14:15.620
I bet you were a little irritated for a moment.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:23.270
It's true that Ogiue-san wouldn't have
come this far if it wasn't for Ohno-san, though.

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:23.990
Yeah.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:29.420
Besides, if it wasn't for Ogiue-san,
the summer Comifes would have been a disaster.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:34.640
I think she wants to make another doujinshi.

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:37.010
Wow, really?

00:14:37.010 --> 00:14:38.130
What makes you think that?

00:14:38.130 --> 00:14:42.000
She's been subtly inquiring about similar topics recently.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.250
She might be thinking about...

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:47.340
Girls sure take the initiative these days.

00:14:47.340 --> 00:14:48.950
Kasubake-san's a good example of that.

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:50.410
She takes it more than she needs to.

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:55.280
Yeah, it'd be nice if she grew up a little.

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:57.810
Her hatred towards otakus is like a...

00:14:57.810 --> 00:14:59.230
fear of people who are close to her.

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:04.110
I know what you mean.
It makes her situation that much more unfortunate.

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:07.330
Well, everyone goes through that phase of their lives.

00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:08.920
Excluding you, Kousaka.

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:12.220
Oh, there you are.

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:17.660
Yeah, I'm full, I'm full!
My stomach's completely full.

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:20.260
Y-You guys are fast.

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:24.900
I started relaxing when I realized that I'd be back tomorrow.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:28.360
No, no! Tomorrow isn't the same as today!

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:30.330
How was the stage?

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:36.280
Typical Sunbeam. They gathered a few young
voice actresses,
created a group, and made them sing.

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:41.250
W-Well, they're p-pretty cute, so it's okay.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:43.180
Was that girl there?

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:47.290
Katou You, the only one who wasn't
replaced when the game was adapted into an anime.

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:49.680
Yeah, she was there.

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:52.040
She looked a little lost on the stage.

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:53.890
She was standing at the far end.

00:15:53.890 --> 00:16:01.130
Wh-While the other girls were making e-eye contact
with the audience, s-she couldn't overcome her nerves.

00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:02.270
Geez.

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:07.060
That's not all. The emcee mentioned
that she was the only one who was retained,

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:11.750
a-and when she tried to reply, s-she made a mistake.

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:16.490
Speaking of which, she resembles Ogichin.

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:20.170
In what way?

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:22.950
Don't you think they look alike? Failure!

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:24.710
Are you talking about the character she voices?

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:25.960
<i>Character?</i>

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:28.320
What was the name of that character again?

00:16:28.690 --> 00:16:31.160
Oh, that's right, Takatera Mishio.

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:34.010
S-She doesn't look like Mishio at all.

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:36.790
Oh, I think I know what you mean.

00:16:38.250 --> 00:16:42.680
He's talking about Mishio's appearance
whenever she's trying her best to fight for her life.

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:47.020
I have a hard time dealing with role characters.

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:49.730
What do you mean by role characters?

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:58.240
Well, characters whose parameters
feature a higher guts level and a lower stress level.

00:16:58.590 --> 00:17:01.050
I can see why you'd have a hard time with her.

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:04.430
Yeah. It only takes one mistake to ruin your progress.

00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:06.700
The same thing goes for Wakumemono's Yuuna.

00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:12.090
Oh, the date with Ogichin should be at Toranoana.

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:18.510
Since she hates otakus, it'd have to be at a
place like Haiburoori, Taruto Shoukai, or Reburo.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:22.470
The appropriate present for her would have to be
something with a subculture following, like a photo book.

00:17:25.280 --> 00:17:28.350
When you visit the legendary tree,
she'll try to hide,

00:17:28.350 --> 00:17:31.270
not realizing that the protagonist has already noticed her.

00:17:31.600 --> 00:17:34.190
She'll try to surprise him
by suddenly showing up,

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:40.390
but by failing to do so,
th-the only thing she'll be able to do is blush.

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:45.600
She'll try to hide her flushed face,
which is when you'd hold her from behind.

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:48.060
A hug, how wonderful.

00:17:48.060 --> 00:17:50.750
You'd hold her in your arms like this.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:55.210
If she says, "Do it",
it's an immediate okay!

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:57.760
Do it.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:11.320
She'll be aggressive even
though it's her first time.

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:18.440
What do they call that in
boy love terminology?
Passive seduction?

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:23.110
Oh, I see,

00:18:23.110 --> 00:18:26.370
not that I see where you
were going with this.

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:30.160
<i>Give me a break!</i>

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:34.880
Kugayama-san, what are you doing?

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:38.410
W-Well, i-isn't this pretty embarrassing?

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:41.970
I-It might be okay here, but on the Chuo Line...

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:46.830
Hey, Kugayama's trying to act like a normal person!

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:48.100
S-Shut up!

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:51.060
I'm going to let it all hang out.

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:53.670
I'll let it hang for the rest of my life.

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:55.980
Geez.

00:18:56.220 --> 00:18:58.000
Kucchii, you should make some effort to hide it.

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:07.030
<i>Shit!</i>

00:19:14.950 --> 00:19:16.630
<i>It's soft.</i>

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:22.680
A-Are you all right?

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:25.790
Well...

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:31.110
Are you...

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:32.040
<i>Shit!</i>

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:33.560
<i>Is that Ohno's voice?</i>

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:36.130
<i>My glasses... Damn, where are my glasses?</i>

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:37.000
Here.

00:19:43.480 --> 00:19:45.820
You came after all, Ogiue-san.

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:49.170
You've got the wrong person.

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:03.220
Let me get that for you.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:07.320
Oh, that circle, huh?

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:09.170
You have good taste.

00:20:09.170 --> 00:20:11.390
You should have come with us from the start.

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:13.600
Oh, it's Ogichin, isn't it?

00:20:14.180 --> 00:20:15.700
No way!

00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:17.070
W-What's she doing here?

00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:20.390
You have some unexpected fetishes!

00:20:20.390 --> 00:20:21.320
What is that?

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:30.730
Oh, she ran away.

00:20:30.730 --> 00:20:32.750
You're not supposed to run.

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:34.120
W-What's going on?

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:37.110
What a typical reaction from her.

00:20:37.110 --> 00:20:38.790
She hasn't grown up at all.

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:49.170
What's this?

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:51.430
It's been here since last year.

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:53.760
It's Ogiue-san's personal belongings.

00:20:53.760 --> 00:20:55.650
Everything in there is hers.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:59.330
That reminds me. I haven't seen Ogiue for a while.

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:00.020
What's with her?

00:21:01.770 --> 00:21:03.610
Who knows?

00:22:37.910 --> 00:22:40.320
I'll repeat myself for the sake of clarification.

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:46.190
I-I want to participate in the summer
Comifes... I mean, I'd like to participate.

00:22:46.190 --> 00:22:51.010
I purchased an application form during the winter Comifes,

00:22:51.700 --> 00:22:53.960
but I didn't know how to fill out the form.

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:58.270
I thought about asking at the
booth during the winter Comifes, but...

00:22:58.900 --> 00:23:01.330
I mean, I couldn't do it.

00:23:01.330 --> 00:23:06.280
I wanted to ask about how I should fill
out the form for the summer Comifes, and...

00:23:06.280 --> 00:23:08.150
Um... Um...

00:23:10.730 --> 00:23:14.090
Ogii, you came to Tokyo from the countryside, right?

00:23:14.090 --> 00:23:14.700
Yes.

00:23:14.700 --> 00:23:17.330
Was there anything in particular
that made you say, "Wow, I'm in Tokyo"?

00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:20.070
Well, the sight of skyscrapers in Shinjuku.

00:23:20.070 --> 00:23:22.120
What about the subways and trains?

00:23:22.120 --> 00:23:22.830
Yeah.

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:26.750
At the beginning, I had to look up the timetable and
routes on the Internet whenever I had to go somewhere.

00:23:26.750 --> 00:23:28.010
Timetables, too?

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:29.270
I know what you mean.

00:23:29.270 --> 00:23:31.190
You tend to panic whenever you miss the train on your route,

00:23:31.190 --> 00:23:33.560
but it isn't even an issue since
the next one arrives relatively quickly.

00:23:33.560 --> 00:23:34.300
Aside from that...

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:38.630
The thought of being able to buy doujinshis at any time, regardless of location, right?
